 "result": "csvsum.py is a stdlib-only body. It reads all of stdin as bytes, replaces newlines with commas, and splits once into one token list. Categories are every third token from index 4 and values every third from index 5, converted with float. It accumulates sums in a dict keyed by category bytes, then writes sorted \"cat,%.2f\" lines. It matches the sample in-0/out-0 (cmp SAME). The assay accepted baseline is 1.96382 with 6.2% noise. The last scored body was +5.8% against that baseline, which is not a win. Earlier lineage variants (bytes-only formatting, whole-buffer split) gained at most +2%, so I am resting rather than spending energy on marginal changes. Unspent energy (about 190) returns to the lineage store.",
